**2. TARGET AUDIENCE**

**Primary Personas**

• Wellness-Oriented Adult — 30–55 yrs, prioritises functional health, reads nutrition labels

• Urban Health Seeker — Follows wellness trends, uses daily functional products

• Quality-First Cook — Chef or home cook who cares deeply about ingredient authenticity

• Gluten-Free / Vegan Consumer — Needs certified-safe options, not just claims

• Established Organic Buyer — Already buys organic, looking for a wide-range trusted brand

**What They Care About**

• Heritage and trust — 20+ years in market is a meaningful signal

• Functional wellness — not just food, but food that does something

• Certification proof — won't accept "natural" without organic certification

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

**3. BRAND VOICE ****&**** TONE**

**Tone Descriptors**

• Authoritative — 20+ years of expertise speaks with earned confidence

• Health-Informed — References nutrition facts, functional benefits, wellness science

• Premium but Approachable — Aspirational quality without sounding elitist

• Warm & Trustworthy — Genuinely cares, not a sales pitch

**Words We Use**

Certified / potent / clinical / ancestral / lab-tested / unadulterated / uncompromising / verified / 250+ tests / APEDA-certified / USDA-approved / since 2003 / two decades / farm-fresh / transparent / trustworthy / chemical-free

**Words We Avoid**

Casual slang / preachy eco-lectures / unsubstantiated claims / timid language / anything Caveman-adjacent in energy / "healthy" used as a vague hook without specifics

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

**4. VISUAL IDENTITY**

**Brand Colours — Canonical Hex Codes**

• Teal Green: #1A6B5A — Primary brand colour (all brand contexts)

• Organic Red: #C0392B — Badge accent, certification marks

• Leaf Green: #2E8B57 — Secondary green, accents

• Sky Blue: #87CEEB — Farm illustration, background accents

• White: #FFFFFF — Badge text, clean UI

| **⚠ FIREFLY COLOUR NOTE** Adobe Firefly prompts use #007878 as the prompt-safe approximation of Teal Green. Use #1A6B5A in all non-Firefly brand contexts. Firefly also uses #003C32 for deep teal depth — this is an acceptable variation for prompt-generated backgrounds only. |
| --- |

**Photography Style**

• Clean, bright natural light — more polished than Pusht, less dark than Caveman

• Farm-field imagery, green crops, open fields — reinforce the "fields" brand name

• Wellness lifestyle: morning routines, yoga, clean eating spreads

• Product flat lays on natural surfaces — linen, marble, aged wood

• Rozana-specific: morning ritual shots, daily habit context

**What to Always Show**

• Teal green as the anchor colour — unique in the organic space

• Farm and field imagery reinforcing the brand name

• Premium, considered composition — more editorial than casual

**What to Never Show**

• Dark, moody, dramatic backgrounds (Caveman territory)

• Overly casual or rough textures

• Unbranded or generic stock-photo feel

